# Template for the navigation package's Debian control file.
#
# Carries over the deb_info block from the vdp-navigation recipe in
# swsoc-elxr-config (boards/arm64/simaai/packages/vdp-navigation/vdp-navigation.yaml).
# Placeholders are substituted by packaging/build-navigation-deb.sh:
#
#   @VERSION@         nav2_bringup/package.xml <version>, plus +<date>.g<sha>
#   @ARCH@            the build host's Debian architecture
#   @INSTALLED_SIZE@  measured from the staged tree
#   @DEPENDS@         dpkg-shlibdeps, plus packaging/runtime-depends.txt
#
# WHY `navigation` AND NOT `vdp-navigation`
#   The eLxr package is versioned with the Palette release number -- 2.1.3 --
#   while this one is versioned with nav2's own, 1.3.12. Keeping the old name
#   would ask apt to accept 1.3.12 as an upgrade of 2.1.3, which it correctly
#   refuses, so a devkit would silently keep the Bitbucket build. A new name
#   plus Conflicts/Replaces makes apt do the right thing: remove the old
#   package, install this one. Provides keeps anything that already
#   `Depends: vdp-navigation` satisfiable.
#
#   Conflicts is kept even though the two no longer share a file. This package
#   installs under /usr/local/navigation while vdp-navigation uses
#   /usr/local/rosbot_navigation, so dpkg would happily hold both -- and that
#   is the problem: two Nav2 installations, two setup files, and whichever the
#   shell happened to source last winning. Conflicts makes apt remove the old
#   one rather than leave an ambiguous board.
#
# Lines beginning with # are stripped before the control file is written.
Package: navigation
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Section: robotics
Priority: optional
Maintainer: SiMa.ai Technologies <noreply@sima.ai>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: @DEPENDS@
Conflicts: vdp-navigation
Replaces: vdp-navigation
Provides: vdp-navigation
Description: SiMa.ai Nav2 / ROS2 Navigation packages
 The ROS 2 Jazzy Navigation2 stack, built natively for arm64 from the
 sima-vertical-solutions/navigation fork and installed under
 /usr/local/navigation. Note this is NOT the /usr/local/rosbot_navigation the
 eLxr package used; anything sourcing that path has to be updated.
 .
 Built with --packages-up-to nav2_bringup nav2_route, which is the closure the
 board actually loads: the planners, controllers, costmap layers, behaviour
 tree, lifecycle manager, route server and their bringup launch files.
 .
 Built from the `jazzy` branch, which is nav2 1.3.12. The fork's default branch
 is `main`, inherited from upstream, and `main` is nav2 1.5.0 -- the Rolling
 development line, which does not match the Jazzy ros2 package this links
 against.
